=== PROPOSAL ===
  ABSTAINED - no permitted action fits the evidence
  if wrong    : This abstention is wrong if the corrected Loki query returns nginx error lines clustered at 05:12:35 naming a specific upstream, or if a Tempo query over an earlier same-day window shows nginx-web-server emitting spans normally — either would convert the empty window into onset evidence and localise a mechanism, at which point restart_service on the named service becomes defensible. It is also wrong if the change-log tool recovers and shows a deploy or config edit on one of the four services inside the window, which would make rollback_image or revert_config the right class. Note that abstention's correctness cannot itself be confirmed by a metric: there is no series that goes green to prove not acting was right, which is part of why acting here would be unverifiable too — with span metrics structurally absent for all four services [tr_ecf722d4c88a, tr_df4845357d16, tr_ff29c4182d6f, tr_0a142cfdc055], no permitted action's effect could be measured as an error ratio falling or a latency percentile returning.
